This page provides a place to discuss new items for inclusion on  [LINK: (In the news) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news]  (ITN),  [LINK: (a protected template) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:In_the_news]  on the  [LINK: (Main Page) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Main_Page]  (see past items  [LINK: (in the ITN archives) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates/Archives] ). Do not report errors in ITN items that are already on the Main Page here— discuss those at  [LINK: (the relevant section of WP:ERRORS) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:ERRORS#Errors_with_"In_the_news"] .

This candidates page is integrated with the daily pages of  [LINK: (Portal:Current events) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portal:Current_events] . A light green header appears under each daily section – it includes transcluded  [LINK: (Portal:Current events) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portal:Current_events]  items for that day. You can discuss ITN candidates under the header.

Vietnam's  [LINK: (communist party congress) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/14th_National_Congress_of_the_Communist_Party_of_Vietnam]  re-elects  [LINK: (Tô Lâm) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%B4_L%C3%A2m]  (pictured) as  [LINK: (general secretary) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Communist_Party_of_Vietnam] , the most powerful position in the  [LINK: (one-party state) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One-party_state] .

[LINK: (Iliana Iotova) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iliana_Iotova]  becomes the first female  [LINK: (president of Bulgaria) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Bulgaria]  following the resignation of  [LINK: (Rumen Radev) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rumen_Radev] .

The United States leaves the  [LINK: (World Health Organization) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Health_Organization] .

