Comment  [LINK: (2026 United States military buildup in the Middle East) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_military_buildup_in_the_Middle_East]  is closely related, and  [LINK: (2026 Iran explosions) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Iran_explosions]  is likely related, but that's not (currently) supported by WP:RS. However: the quality of 2026 United States military buildup in the Middle East is weak (it needs heavy copyediting); and 2026 Iran explosions is for the moment not much more than a stub, and the sources don't assert a direct relation between the protests and the explosions - they only describe the explosions as happening within the general context of the protests. If the social media claims of about a dozen explosions on 31 Jan 2026 rather than just two become supported by WP:RS, then 2026 Iran explosions could become ITN relevant, even without formally being related to the protests. If the quality of 2026 United States military buildup in the Middle East improves sufficiently, then it could qualify for ITN. There's also  [LINK: (Draft:2026 United States-Iran crisis) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Draft:2026_United_States-Iran_crisis] , which needs a lot of work before moving to mainspace.  [LINK: (Boud) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Boud]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Boud] )  [LINK: (18:06, 31 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates#c-Boud-20260131180600-GreatCaesarsGhost-20260130122300] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates] ]


