That's a good argument, I didn't consider it that way. Our article is about the 'hostage crisis' as a whole, but the blurb is about a specific event. If the level of detail by sources on the specific event is relatively small and they're just using it as a reason to talk about 'bigger' topics, then it might not be a great blurb. I'm switching to neutral, also in part because we have featured this article before and I think we meet ITNPURPOSE better if we feature different articles over time. Still don't think it's a bad feature, for what it's worth, but there may be better ones in the future. ~ [LINK: (Maplestrip/Mable) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Maplestrip]  ( [LINK: (chat) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Maplestrip] )  [LINK: (08:54, 29 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates#c-Maplestrip-20260129085400-EvansHallBear-20260128203600] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates] ]
If the level of detail by sources on the specific event is relatively small and they're just using it as a reason to talk about 'bigger' topics, then it might not be a great blurb. All of the support arguments here are following this logic as well by focusing on the hostage crisis or peace process more broadly while failing to address the specific event. Obviously the hostage crisis was significant, as was the ceasefire agreement that returned the hostages that military action could not. But the returning of the last hostage is largely symbolic (except for to the family/friends of the deceased who can finally get closure). It does not inherit significance from the broader war/hostage crisis.  [LINK: (EvansHallBear) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:EvansHallBear]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:EvansHallBear] )  [LINK: (17:49, 30 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates#c-EvansHallBear-20260130174900-Maplestrip-20260129085400] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates] ]

