@ [LINK: (Masem) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Masem]  The standards be contended here are completely arbitrary. People are saying that they don't care about the story personally (not relevant), that they think all stories of that type are unimportant but don't engage with the specifics of the story at hand (unproductive and unhelpful), or that it's most/more relevant to a single country, usually one they personally don't care about (not important or relevant). So many oppose arguments in discussions, including this one, are just a form of saying "who cares?" without any elaboration. It's borderline disruptive.  [LINK: (AaronNealLucas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Aplucas0703]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Aplucas0703] )  [LINK: (21:24, 28 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates#c-Aplucas0703-20260128212400-Masem-20260126044200] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates] ]
