Moving over from wait to support alt3 - no less significant than the Chilean wildfires in ITN right now. I have to say some of the oppose rationales above are some of the most extreme "minimum deaths" arguments I've seen at ITN -- opposing because the deaths are a relatively small percent of the entire population of North America ("28 deaths is not an extraordinary number for a continent with more than 500 million inhabitants") or significantly smaller than the total number of people who die of all possible causes daily in North America ("About 10,000 people die every day in North America from a variety of causes.  10 more random deaths are just snowflakes in the storm.") is insane. If deaths as a proportion of the total population is something we start caring about here, then the bar is 10x higher for events in Asia because 100,000 die there every day. I certainly hope we never have a blurb that passes a threshold like that. I think this topic meets the much more sensible bar of "major event occurring in multiple countries, of interest to readers, widely covered in the news, and with a quality Wikipedia article to showcase."  [LINK: (Vanilla) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Vanilla_Wizard]  [LINK: (Wizard) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Vanilla_Wizard]   [LINK: (💙) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Contributions/Vanilla_Wizard]   [LINK: (01:37, 27 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates#c-Vanilla_Wizard-20260127013700-Chorchapu-20260125185200] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates] ]

