Sources?  Statistics? The article currently claims 50 fatalities but there's no source provided for this, so far as I can see.  The nomination doesn't list any sources either.  And, when you look at the detail, the attribution of the deaths seems fairly sweeping: a child is killed when towed on a sled; a tree falls on a mobile home; some homeless die in the open; someone is hit by a snowplough truck.  Such misadventurous and accidental deaths happen throughout the year but are being counted here if there's a vague connection with the snow.  These are not good statistics.  See  [LINK: (excess mortality) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Excess_mortality] .  [LINK: (Andrew) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Andrew_Davidson] 🐉( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Andrew_Davidson] )  [LINK: (08:27, 27 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates#c-Andrew_Davidson-20260127082700-Chorchapu-20260125185200] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates] ]
