Support alt3 in principle, though there are two orange tags in the article. This goes beyond a normal winter storm, setting snowfall records and extending into regions that don't normally receive any. 106 deaths is substantial. It made sense to wait a few days ago, but the impact is now clear, if not over.  [LINK: (Modest Genius) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Modest_Genius]   [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Modest_Genius]   [LINK: (19:22, 29 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates#c-Modest_Genius-20260129192200-Chorchapu-20260125185200] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates] ]

Support alt3. Probably not quite as noteworthy as the Texas ice storm of a few years ago, and maybe not even the gulf coast system last year (which was less impactful but noteworthy for it's location), but the impact of this system is far from a frequent occurrence. High fatalities, large-scale disruptions of travel, countless power outages, and likely a decent degree of financial damage. Lots of boxes checked here.  [LINK: (DarkSide830) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:DarkSide830]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:DarkSide830] )  [LINK: (01:25, 30 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates#c-DarkSide830-20260130012500-Chorchapu-20260125185200] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates] ]

