We should cover it because it's in the news, of course.  The fact that it has been running for some time means that we have quite a substantial article now -- the article has about 80 sources and it is graded as  [LINK: (vital) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:VITAL] .  But ITN doesn't seem to have ever posted anything about it and, now it has reached the top echelons, it seems a good time to let people know what's going on.  This also fits well with the general zeitgeist about China's growing strength, threats to Taiwan, autocratic example and so forth.  [LINK: (Andrew) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Andrew_Davidson] 🐉( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Andrew_Davidson] )  [LINK: (16:16, 24 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates#c-Andrew_Davidson-20260124161600-Masem-20260124130100] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates] ]

