Oppose According to WSJ ([9]), he is being accused of leaking info to the US. Assuming WSJ is accurate, "spy gets caught" is not ITN worthy.  [LINK: (Jumpytoo) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Jumpytoo]   [LINK: (Talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Jumpytoo]   [LINK: (19:45, 25 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates#c-Jumpytoo-20260125194500-Andrew_Davidson-20260124101900] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates] ]
Seems an unlikely allegation to me.  In the Soviet purges, the people who were given  [LINK: (show trials) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Show_trial]  were commonly tortured to induce such outlandish confessions.   See the  [LINK: (Moscow trials) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow_trials]  for the unpleasant details.  Anyway, the more bizarre the allegations, the more notable the matter becomes.  [LINK: (Andrew) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Andrew_Davidson] 🐉( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Andrew_Davidson] )  [LINK: (20:01, 25 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates#c-Andrew_Davidson-20260125200100-Jumpytoo-20260125194500] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates] ]
Looking around, the FT has a different account including a statement that he had “severely trampled on and damaged the chairman responsibility system”, "suggesting that ensuring the powers of the Chinese leader is behind a probe of Zhang Youxia announced on Saturday, rather than just charges of corruption".
The FT goes on to provide a variety of analyses from various experts on the history of these purges and factional politics.  This level of detailed expert coverage further demonstrates the notability of the matter.
