Support altblurb Widely reported in news around the world and significant in the context of tensions with Taiwan. The notability of the key players is clear: Zhang Youxia is the highest-ranked general in Xi Jinping's inner circle as the leader of China's supreme military leadership body (the Central Military Commission aka CMC), and his suspension and arrest are consequential in demonstrating Xi's centralisation of power in the CCP around himself alone.  Where historically the removal of top officials perceived to threaten the leader was often swept under the rug and Chinese newspapers heavily censored any discussion about their fate (see the Lin Biao incident in 1971), this event is unusually public and it is no secret that Zhang Youxia's fall from power has become a major news story both within China and worldwide.  [LINK: (Oppius Brutus) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Oppius_Brutus]   [LINK: (03:57, 26 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates#c-Oppius_Brutus-20260126035700-Andrew_Davidson-20260124101900] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates] ]

