Wait Something is happening, but it remains unclear what. The CCP has released the barest of confirmations: Zhang has been 'suspended' due to 'serious violations of discipline and law' possibly linked to an 'anti-corruption campaign.' RS do not seem clear on what actually happened and why it matters. Some have gone so far to suggest that Zhang was involved in a coup attempt. ITN shouldn't echo CCP talking points and shouldn't rush a blurb.  [LINK: (Dr Fell) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=User:Dr_Fell&action=edit&redlink=1]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Dr_Fell] )  [LINK: (07:11, 27 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates#c-Dr_Fell-20260127071100-Andrew_Davidson-20260124101900] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates] ]
Coup bits come from rumour mills online, haven't seen any RS report on that. What they do report however is that this is the most significant purge since the Mao era. CCP authorities "investigating" top CCP leaders is just doublespeak for removals/purges (be they for corruption or political). As is routine, Zhang would be removed from the CMC and expelled from the party in sometime but the impact of it being "in the news" would be largely over by then.  [LINK: (Gotitbro) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Gotitbro]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Gotitbro] )  [LINK: (08:09, 27 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates#c-Gotitbro-20260127080900-Dr_Fell-20260127071100] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates] ]
Sky News (not AU) was reporting on the alleged coup. I do agree that this is the most significant purge since Mao and that the CCP's language is deliberately opaque and should not be parroted. I'm not opposed to a blurb on his removal but careful verbiage is needed.  [LINK: (Dr Fell) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=User:Dr_Fell&action=edit&redlink=1]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Dr_Fell] )  [LINK: (08:24, 27 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates#c-Dr_Fell-20260127082400-Gotitbro-20260127080900] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:In_the_news/Candidates] ]

The BBC has further coverage: China has purged its highest-ranked military general. Why?  This makes it clear that Zhang is out and that "investigation almost certainly means being given a custodial sentence as a minimum".  But the details of what happened to cause the breach are unclear and so there's lots of speculation.  See also further analysis in other sources such as ABC, CNN and the Institut Montaigne.

